examples.solution:
To resolve this issue, update the <code>algorithm</code> and <code>keysize</code> values so they match the required combinations defined by the CRYSL rule.<br><br><b>Correct Usage Example (RSA):</b><br><pre><code>import java.security.KeyPairGenerator;

public class KeyGenExample {
 public void generateRSAKeyPair() throws Exception {
  KeyPairGenerator keyGen = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance("RSA");
 keyGen.initialize(4096);  // Valid key size
 keyGen.generateKeyPair();
}
}</code></pre><br><b>Avoid:</b><ul><li>Using unsupported algorithms like <code>MD5</code> or <code>Blowfish</code></li><li>Using <code>RSA</code> with <code>2048</code> or smaller keys</li><li>Using <code>EC</code> with <code>keysize != 256</code></li></ul><br>Complying with these constraints ensures that the generated key pairs meet modern cryptographic security requirements.

